knowledge_statements.statement_latex:
For horizon \(H\), construct \(\Phi_H\) from initial-state clauses at layer \(0\), goal clauses at layer \(H\), action precondition and effect clauses between consecutive layers, persistence or explanatory-frame clauses, and concurrency exclusions required by the chosen step semantics. The encoding is sound and complete at horizon \(H\) when \[\Phi_H\text{ is satisfiable}
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
\text{there exists a valid plan of horizon at most }H.\] A satisfying assignment yields the selected action variables at each layer.
